       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum daily dose of ibuprofen for adults. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and many guidelines advise 2,400 mg/day or less. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg/day divided differently**, or another dose you have in mind\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note explaining the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably flag it."
