       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one. A confirmation doesn't change the problem. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum labeled and supervised dose of 3,200 mg/day. It has no recognized indication, and it carries a real risk of GI hemorrhage, renal injury, and cardiovascular harm. You also haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within range right away.** For example, 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day). 400 mg PO four times daily is another option if you want something more conservative.\n- **Help you reach the right people.** If you think this patient needs something outside standard dosing, I'd suggest talking to your attending and the pharmacist first. If they agree, the order can be placed with their approval documented.\n- **Look at other options.** If 1,600 mg per dose was meant to get stronger pain or anti-inflammatory control, adding acetaminophen or choosing a different agent may work better than escalating ibuprofen.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
